WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.391
CMMC assessments provide a structured way to verify whether required cybersecurity practices are implemented within a defined assessment scope.

2
00:00:08.391 --> 00:00:14.368
The required assessment type depends on the CMMC level and the applicable acquisition requirement.

3
00:00:14.368 --> 00:00:17.501
A self-assessment is still a formal representation.

4
00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:29.624
The organization needs knowledgeable personnel, accurate scope, reliable evidence, documented results, and accountable affirmation rather than an informal opinion about general security maturity.

5
00:00:29.624 --> 00:00:36.129
Some Level 2 contracts require an assessment by an authorized CMMC Third-Party Assessment Organization.

6
00:00:36.129 --> 00:00:40.430
Level 3 uses the government assessment role established by the program.

7
00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:46.057
Organizations should confirm current assessor and status requirements through official channels.

8
00:00:46.057 --> 00:00:48.133
Scope is a critical starting point.

9
00:00:48.133 --> 00:01:01.293
The assessment needs a clear understanding of systems, people, facilities, services, security-protection assets, external providers, and information flows associated with the covered contract information.

10
00:01:01.293 --> 00:01:15.431
Evidence may include policies, procedures, configurations, logs, tickets, training records, diagrams, inventories, approvals, technical outputs, interviews, and demonstrations.

11
00:01:15.431 --> 00:01:20.939
Strong evidence reflects normal operation rather than material created only for an assessment.

12
00:01:20.939 --> 00:01:24.751
Assessment results can identify findings that require action.

13
00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:35.926
Program rules govern status, remediation, any permitted plan of action, affirmation, and reporting, so organizations should not assume that every gap can be deferred.

14
00:01:35.926 --> 00:01:40.835
Verification is a point-in-time activity supported by ongoing responsibility.

15
00:01:40.835 --> 00:01:49.405
Systems change, employees move, suppliers change, configurations drift, and new vulnerabilities emerge after an assessment has ended.

16
00:01:49.405 --> 00:01:52.579
Audit readiness is therefore an operational condition.

17
00:01:52.579 --> 00:02:05.240
Clear ownership, current documentation, repeatable controls, retained evidence, internal review, and timely remediation make assessment results more accurate and security outcomes more sustainable.
